{"orgCode":"7300","name":"Agricultural Labor Relations Board","agencyCode":"7000","agencyName":"Labor and Workforce Development","description":"The Agricultural Labor Relations Board is responsible for: (1) carrying out the policy of the State of California to encourage and protect the associational rights of agricultural employees; (2) protecting California farm workers' right to decide through a secret ballot election or a showing of majority support to have a union represent them in collective bargaining with their employer; and (3) investigating, prosecuting, and adjudicating unfair labor practice disputes.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":15309,"cy":20089,"by":21613},"positions":{"py":61.6,"cy":80,"by":84}},"programs":{"id":"exp/7000/7300","kind":"department","name":"Agricultural Labor Relations Board","code":"7300","amounts":{"py":15309,"cy":20089,"by":21613},"positions":{"py":61.6,"cy":80,"by":84},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":11185,"cy":11645,"by":11815},"special":{"py":4124,"cy":8444,"by":9798}},"children":[{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6050","kind":"program","name":"Board Administration","code":"6050","amounts":{"py":3414,"cy":4332,"by":4390},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3294,"cy":3483,"by":3541},"special":{"py":120,"cy":849,"by":849}},"positions":{"py":14.5,"cy":17,"by":17},"description":"6050 - BOARD ADMINISTRATION\n\nThe main objective of the Office of the Board is to administer, interpret, and enforce the Agricultural Labor Relations Act. The Office of the Board holds evidentiary hearings and adjudicates disputes in unfair labor practice cases, as well as disputes arising out of representation elections. The Office of the Board also administers the mandatory mediation law and is vested with the authority to promulgate regulations to implement the Act. When required, the Office of the Board initiates and oversees litigation before the Courts of Appeal and grants authority to the General Counsel to take action in Superior Court. The Board, where appropriate, conducts education and outreach activities.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3414,"cy":4332,"by":4390}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6050/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":3294,"cy":3483,"by":3541},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3294,"cy":3483,"by":3541}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3294,"cy":3483,"by":3541}}}},{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6050/f3078","kind":"fund","name":"Labor and Workforce Development Fund","code":"3078","amounts":{"py":120,"cy":849,"by":849},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":120,"cy":849,"by":849}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":120,"cy":849,"by":849}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6055","kind":"program","name":"General Counsel Administration","code":"6055","amounts":{"py":9629,"cy":13192,"by":13335},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":6226,"cy":6409,"by":6520},"special":{"py":3403,"cy":6783,"by":6815}},"positions":{"py":42.9,"cy":55,"by":55},"description":"6055 - GENERAL COUNSEL ADMINISTRATION\n\nThe Office of the General Counsel is the Agricultural Labor Relations Board's chief prosecutor. The General Counsel's responsibility includes enforcing the Agricultural Labor Relations Act in unfair labor practice proceedings before the Board, supervising and coordinating personnel in regional offices who are responsible for investigating unfair labor practice charges and other matters, prosecuting unfair labor practice cases, settling or dismissing cases where appropriate, conducting elections, and seeking compliance with final Board orders. The General Counsel's office supervises and oversees litigation before administrative law judges, the Board and, when necessary, the Superior Courts. The General Counsel's office also conducts education and outreach activities on behalf of the Office of the Board.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":9629,"cy":13192,"by":13335}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6055/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":6226,"cy":6409,"by":6520},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":6226,"cy":6409,"by":6520}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":6226,"cy":6409,"by":6520}}}},{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6055/f3078","kind":"fund","name":"Labor and Workforce Development Fund","code":"3078","amounts":{"py":3403,"cy":6783,"by":6815},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":3403,"cy":6783,"by":6815}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3403,"cy":6783,"by":6815}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6060","kind":"program","name":"Administration","code":"6060","amounts":{"py":2266,"cy":2565,"by":3888},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1665,"cy":1753,"by":1754},"special":{"py":601,"cy":812,"by":2134}},"positions":{"py":4.2,"cy":8,"by":12},"description":"6060 - ADMINISTRATION\n\nThe objective of the Division of Administrative Services is to support operations to enable the programs to accomplish statutory mandates in an effective and efficient manner, through the services provided by accounting, budget, human resource management, business services, procurement and contracting, fiscal accountability, information technology infrastructure, and other administrative services.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2266,"cy":2565,"by":3888}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6060/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":1665,"cy":1753,"by":1754},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1665,"cy":1753,"by":1754}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1665,"cy":1753,"by":1754}}}},{"id":"exp/7000/7300/6060/f3078","kind":"fund","name":"Labor and Workforce Development Fund","code":"3078","amounts":{"py":601,"cy":812,"by":2134},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":601,"cy":812,"by":2134}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Op